    "done_when": "Continue from the committed receipt at docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/repaired-remeasure-receipt/ (its review: /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reviews/nova/r-20261003T132000326731-cco-repaired-constrained-remeasure-receipt.json, 88/100, fail only because positive.json carries four accepted Newton promotions with global residuals but no row-residual series). A committed driver under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/row-history-receipt/ runs as ONE fresh H200 job (betelgeuse, reservation gpu_0003_grpA, one card, 8 CPUs, --mem=128G, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova/.venv/bin/python without uv, clip_mode=exact passed explicitly, submitted with RECKON_ALLOW_NESTED_LAUNCH=1 sbatch, never srun or salloc) on the same weak-rotation-reactor-static 110-cell positive arm from the same displaced seed, and writes row-history.json holding one entry per accepted Newton promotion with the global residual, the first-moment row residual in pitches against the derived tolerance (1.66e-4 pitches), and the compensating amplitudes. The final entry must reproduce the committed terminal values (global 2.68e-14, row 9.53e-15 pitches, positive state binary64 SHA256 0196d8cce7b0f3c5b7852bcc0e42ecd7ac154a3b5e11f81fedea8fe6bd77e04b), and each entry global residual must match the committed newton_history entry for the same promotion; a mismatch is reported, not tolerated. One hint, a guess and not a finding: a solve stopped after k promotions from the same seed should reproduce promotion k of the full solve when the solve is deterministic, and the global-residual match above is what tests that. If the per-promotion row cannot be observed without editing solver source under nova/, stop and report which solver output is missing; do not edit nova/. Redraw the shared-level flux panel from the committed terminal state with the analytic and solved magnetic-axis markers distinguishable when the P